    },
    "body": "I was just trying to say that, before your PR, I don't see any other place where we would inherit COOP according to policy container rules. For example, if A creates a data url child iframe, I don't think there is any mechanism, before your PR, to have the data url iframe inherit COOP from A. Your PR changes that, because the general policy container inheritance mechanism kicks in. So I am just saying, if we want to make this PR a no-op, would it make sense to change the inheritance algorithm of the policy container so that COOP is *never* inherited? This would avoid the special handling of srcdoc here. And we could sort out the correct inheritance in a separate PR.",
